The field's text goes to libc system(); trueResult on exit 0, falseResult otherwise; no escaping, no output capture.

R1: a fleet row never opens a window or an app. These rows drive harmless commands only.

ST true    system("true") answers trueResult, which prints 1.
ST false   system("false") answers falseResult, which prints 0 -- the zero row's non-zero sibling is ST true.
ST write   a command that writes a file; pop.sh sets SYSTEMT_OUT to a file in its own temp directory and reads it
           back, so the row proves the command ran, not only that something answered 1.

Run alone, SYSTEMT_OUT is unset and the write row's shell redirect fails, so it prints 0.
